From 20260813-susfs-uname Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Pulsar Bot <pulsar@localhost>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 13:40:00 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] susfs: adapt spoof_uname hook to Pulsar 4.19 uname

The Pulsar 4.19 base already carries its own uname spoofing logic, so the
original SuSFS hunk does not match the current function body.  Insert the
SuSFS hook into that existing implementation without replacing it.

Signed-off-by: Pulsar Bot <pulsar@localhost>
---
 kernel/sys.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel/sys.c b/kernel/sys.c
--- a/kernel/sys.c
+++ b/kernel/sys.c
@@ -1240,6 +1240,9 @@ static int override_release(char __user *release, size_t len)
 	return ret;
 }
 
+#ifdef CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_SPOOF_UNAME
+extern void susfs_spoof_uname(struct new_utsname *tmp);
+#endif
 SYSCALL_DEFINE1(newuname, struct new_utsname __user *, name)
 {
 	struct new_utsname tmp;
@@ -1249,6 +1252,8 @@ SYSCALL_DEFINE1(newuname, struct new_utsname __user *, name)
 
 	down_read(&uts_sem);
 	memcpy(&tmp, utsname(), sizeof(tmp));
+#ifdef CONFIG_KSU_SUSFS_SPOOF_UNAME
+	susfs_spoof_uname(&tmp);
+#endif
 	if (cur_uid == 0 &&
 		(!strncmp(current->comm, "bpfloader", 9) ||
